{"applied_rules": [{"rule": "mode+effort_routing", "cell": "judge-local+effort", "detail": "confirmed on holdout: ratio=0.6, ci95=[0.5, 0.75], quality_delta=+0"}], "notes": ["judge backend: judge-jev+effort also confirmed with decision latency within the 500ms budget -- recommend `backend: auto` semantics (jev when TYPESAFE_API_KEY is present AND allow_external_state is explicitly set by the operator, else local); NOT applied here -- external state stays opt-in (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e)).", "model_routing: keep off -- routing cell not present in this results.json.", "external state (privacy): remains opt-in regardless of any result above (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e), docs/PRIVACY.md)."], "diff": {"behaviors/fast-decisions-active.yaml": "--- a/behaviors/fast-decisions-active.yaml\n+++ b/behaviors/fast-decisions-active.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# judge backend: judge-jev+effort also confirmed with decision latency within the 500ms budget -- recommend `backend: auto` semantics (jev when TYPESAFE_API_KEY is present AND allow_external_state is explicitly set by the operator, else local); NOT applied here -- external state stays opt-in (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e)).\n+# model_routing: keep off -- routing cell not present in this results.json.\n+# external state (privacy): remains opt-in regardless of any result above (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e), docs/PRIVACY.md).\n+\n+bundle:\n+  name: fast-decisions-active\n+  version: 0.1.0\n+  description: GENERATED by evals/apply_recommendation.py from a confirmed holdout\n+    result -- see evals/DESIGN-BRIDGE.md. Opt-in active orchestrator profile; composes\n+    on top of bundle.md's shadow default, does not replace it.\n+session:\n+  orchestrator:\n+    module: loop-fast-decisions\n+    source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/loop-fast-decisions\n+    config:\n+      mode: active\n+      backend: ollama\n+      model: qwen3:0.6b\n+      effort_routing:\n+        orient: medium\n+        explore: low\n+        implement: high\n", "behaviors/fast-decisions.yaml": "--- a/behaviors/fast-decisions.yaml\n+++ b/behaviors/fast-decisions.yaml\n@@ -1,50 +1,26 @@\n bundle:\n   name: fast-decisions-behavior\n   version: 0.2.0\n-  description: >-\n-    Orchestrator-primary fast-decisions: replaces the host's orchestrator with\n-    loop-fast-decisions, which wraps the same upstream loop-streaming loop\n-    (steering, approvals, compaction, cancellation, provider pin all stay\n-    upstream's) and decides once per turn whether it is easy (cheaper start\n-    model, one effort level) or hard (the host model, unchanged).\n-    Also mounts the telemetry hook and the read-only fast_workspace tool, and\n-    launches the observatory dashboard on session start.\n-\n-# Why a behavior carries session.orchestrator (deliberately, against the\n-# usual \"behaviors don't pick the orchestrator\" convention): the only seam\n-# that can change a turn is the provider call inside the orchestrator --\n-# upstream never honors a hook's `modify` at tool:pre (see router.py and\n-# docs/UPSTREAM_CONTRACT.md). Composed AFTER a root (bundle.md's include\n-# order, or `amplifier bundle add --app`), the kernel's deep merge makes this\n-# module win while the root's own loop-streaming settings (e.g. foundation's\n-# extended_thinking) are forwarded to the wrapped loop. Delegated sub-sessions\n-# inherit the parent's orchestrator, so routing applies to them too. Want\n-# measurement without the swap? Compose behaviors/fast-decisions-shadow.yaml.\n+  description: 'Orchestrator-primary fast-decisions: replaces the host''s orchestrator\n+    with loop-fast-decisions, which wraps the same upstream loop-streaming loop (steering,\n+    approvals, compaction, cancellation, provider pin all stay upstream''s) and decides\n+    once per turn whether it is easy (cheaper start model, one effort level) or hard\n+    (the host model, unchanged). Also mounts the telemetry hook and the read-only\n+    fast_workspace tool, and launches the observatory dashboard on session start.'\n includes:\n-  - bundle: fast-decisions:behaviors/jevgrep\n-\n+- bundle: fast-decisions:behaviors/jevgrep\n session:\n   orchestrator:\n     module: loop-fast-decisions\n     source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/loop-fast-decisions\n     config:\n       mode: active\n-      # Turn-start difficulty router (evals/STUDY-DESIGN.md 18.7): one typed\n-      # simple/complex question per turn picks model AND effort for the whole\n-      # turn -- simple: cheap start model at one effort; complex: the host\n-      # model at provider-default effort, exactly plain Amplifier. No\n-      # mid-turn switches, so the prompt cache is never re-written.\n-      # Jev is the default judge after the local/hosted Laya quality screen.\n-      # Missing/uncertain/failed decisions retain the normal routing fallback;\n-      # native approvals and confidence gates remain unchanged. AnyJev is opt-in\n-      # only and is not selected by this behavior.\n       backend: jev\n       allow_external_state: true\n-      # The judged read shortcut stays off: it rarely fired in the studies and\n-      # would put a scoring call in front of every slow request.\n       read_shortcut: false\n       timeout_ms: 3000\n-      allowed_tools: [fast_workspace]\n+      allowed_tools:\n+      - fast_workspace\n       effort_routing:\n         orient: medium\n         explore: low\n@@ -54,88 +30,20 @@\n           strong: null\n         max_explore_requests: 6\n         escalate_after_provider_errors: 1\n-      # Research levers (default off; see src/amplifier_fast_decisions/routing_levers.py):\n-      # one knob, profile: frugal | balanced | careful (balanced = this file),\n-      # or the individual model_routing keys tiers / large_repo / strong_effort.\n-      # profile: balanced\n-      # Per-step action set (default off; src/amplifier_fast_decisions/step_actions.py):\n-      # before every model call inside a turn, classify the step from the last\n-      # tool calls/results and pick a prepared read-only action (file window,\n-      # whole file, git status summary -- judged by Jev next_action, asked only\n-      # when the expected saving beats its ~0.15 s), a cheaper model for this\n-      # step only when price- and cache-aware math says it is cheaper, or the\n-      # full model. Every decision leaves a fast_decisions:efficiency receipt.\n-      # step_actions:\n-      #   prepared: true\n-      #   cheaper_model: true      # rarely fires with an Opus 5.5 host (cheap cache reads)\n       model_routing:\n         start_model: claude-sonnet-5\n-        # Only ever send the Anthropic start model to Anthropic providers.\n         provider_match: anthropic\n         start_policy: judge\n-        # Quality-safe scope gate (STUDY-DESIGN.md 18.8): in a workspace with\n-        # more files than this, the turn starts on the host model whatever the\n-        # judge says. On SWE-bench repositories cheap-first lost quality\n-        # (19/30 vs plain 23/30) and escalation did not recover a misdirected\n-        # start. Raise or remove it to trade quality risk for speed on repos.\n         cheap_max_workspace_files: 300\n-        # Decide once: a turn judged easy stays on the start model for the whole\n-        # turn. Switching mid-turn rebuilds the provider's prompt cache (the\n-        # first version was 1.2x slower and 1.4x costlier for it), and in live\n-        # sessions a 6-request limit moved most easy-turn work back to the host\n-        # model. Only a provider error on the start model moves the turn up.\n         max_requests_before_escalation: null\n         escalate_on_test_failure: false\n         escalate_on_provider_error: true\n-        # HC12 (\"easy-turn shaping\", opt-in, disabled by default): on a turn\n-        # judged easy, a cheap model can still burn extra provider round\n-        # trips on ceremony (one `todo` call, one `python_check` call, one\n-        # tool per response) where the host model batches independent tool\n-        # calls into one response and verifies once. Appending guidance to\n-        # the END of the system prompt keeps every call of the turn\n-        # byte-identical (cache-friendly); hiding tools by name removes them\n-        # from just that call's advertised tool list. Left commented out\n-        # until a benchmark shows it helps -- uncomment to enable:\n-        # easy_turn_guidance: >-\n-        #   This request was judged small. Work directly: read what you need\n-        #   in one step, make independent tool calls together in a single\n-        #   response, skip planning and checklist tools, verify once, then\n-        #   give a short answer.\n-        # easy_turn_hide_tools: [todo]\n-      # Cache keep-alive (levers.py): while a tool or helper runs past 270 s\n-      # since the prompt cache was last used, re-send the last request\n-      # unchanged with a 1-token output cap so the next call reads the cache\n-      # instead of re-writing it. Anthropic only; skipped under manual\n-      # extended thinking; at most 6 refreshes per wait; only when >= 20k\n-      # unshared prefix tokens are at risk. Every wait leaves a\n-      # cache_keepalive receipt. Measured (evals/levers-2026-09-25): a 330 s\n-      # bash wait saved $0.16 per run, receipts within $0.0001 of measured.\n-      # Turn off with cache_keepalive: {enabled: false}.\n       cache_keepalive:\n         enabled: true\n         interval_s: 270\n         max_refreshes: 6\n         min_prefix_tokens: 20000\n         max_output_tokens: 1\n-      # Loop-stop nudges (loop_stop) stay off: their receipts did not reconcile with a\n-      # measured A/B (evals/levers-2026-09-25). The waste guards below replace\n-      # them; with both on, the nudges stand down.\n-      # Waste guards (docs/WASTE-GUARDS.md; measured in docs/evidence/\n-      # 2026-09-25/waste-census): deterministic per-tool-call checks, on in\n-      # every session regardless of repo size (the scope gate above decides\n-      # model routing only). Each firing leaves an efficiency receipt.\n-      #  - repeat stop: a call whose last 3 runs returned identical output\n-      #    with nothing changed is not run a fourth time (the model is told\n-      #    to use the earlier result; issuing it again runs it);\n-      #  - retry stop: a command that failed twice with the same error and\n-      #    nothing changed is not run a third time (transient errors exempt);\n-      #  - poll wait: a repeated `sleep N && <read-only check>` is run in place\n-      #    until a finish word appears or progress settles, at most 240 s;\n-      #  - unchanged output: a second identical read/search/command output, or\n-      #    a re-read of an unchanged file range already in context, is\n-      #    returned as a one-line pointer instead of a second copy.\n-      # Turn all off: waste_guards: {enabled: false}; one off, e.g.\n-      # waste_guards: {enabled: true, poll_wait: false}.\n       waste_guards:\n         enabled: true\n         repeat_stop: true\n@@ -143,39 +51,27 @@\n         poll_wait: true\n         identical_results: true\n         poll_max_wait_s: 240\n-      # Auto-observatory: on the top-level session's first session:start,\n-      # reuse-or-spawn a detached `afast serve` and open it. Skipped for\n-      # child sessions, when AFAST_OBSERVATORY=off or AMPLIFIER_NO_BROWSER=1,\n-      # or without a TTY. Stop it with `afast serve --stop`.\n       observatory:\n         enabled: true\n         open_browser: always\n         port: 8765\n-\n hooks:\n-  - module: hooks-fast-decisions\n-    source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/hooks-fast-decisions\n-    config:\n-      # Native-event bridge + session presence for the dashboard. The\n-      # orchestrator owns the decision policy; shadow scoring and the role\n-      # router stand down automatically when it is mounted.\n-      mode: shadow\n-      backend: deterministic\n-      allow_external_state: false\n-      observatory:\n-        enabled: true\n-        open_browser: always\n-        port: 8765\n-\n+- module: hooks-fast-decisions\n+  source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/hooks-fast-decisions\n+  config:\n+    mode: active\n+    backend: ollama\n+    allow_external_state: false\n+    observatory:\n+      enabled: true\n+      open_browser: always\n+      port: 8765\n context:\n   include:\n-    # \"make my amplifier faster\" / \"speed up amplifier\" trigger: hands off to\n-    # the make-amplifier-faster recipe instead of installing anything directly.\n-    - fast-decisions:context/make-faster.md\n-\n+  - fast-decisions:context/make-faster.md\n tools:\n-  - module: tool-fast-workspace\n-    source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/tool-fast-workspace\n-    config:\n-      root: .\n-      max_bytes: 32768\n+- module: tool-fast-workspace\n+  source: git+https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-bundle-fast-decisions@main#subdirectory=modules/tool-fast-workspace\n+  config:\n+    root: .\n+    max_bytes: 32768\n"}, "changelog": "# fast-decisions: apply confirmed evaluation recommendation\n\nApplied (confirmed evidence only):\n- mode+effort_routing (judge-local+effort): confirmed on holdout: ratio=0.6, ci95=[0.5, 0.75], quality_delta=+0\n\nNotes (not applied -- for human ratification):\n- judge backend: judge-jev+effort also confirmed with decision latency within the 500ms budget -- recommend `backend: auto` semantics (jev when TYPESAFE_API_KEY is present AND allow_external_state is explicitly set by the operator, else local); NOT applied here -- external state stays opt-in (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e)).\n- model_routing: keep off -- routing cell not present in this results.json.\n- external state (privacy): remains opt-in regardless of any result above (DESIGN-BRIDGE.md rule (e), docs/PRIVACY.md).\n", "applied": true, "exit": 0, "reason": "applied"}
